[38;5;231m[48;5;238m❯ How do I do the recordings and give it to you? Give me each and every step[39m                                                                                                                                                                                  
[49m                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              
  The idea is to keep the app running in one tmux window and run the recorder from a second window. The recorder points at the app's pane by id, so it doesn't disturb the screen.                                                                            
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              
  [1m1. Make two windows.[0m Inside tmux, window 1 is for the app. Press [38;5;153mprefix + c[39m to open window 2, which is for the recorder. In window 2, run [38;5;153mcd ~/project/terminal-project/regionsel[39m.                                                                          
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              
  [1m2. Find the app pane's id.[0m Start the app in window 1 first, then run this from window 2:                                                                                                                                                                    
  tmux list-panes -a -F [31m'#{pane_id}  #{window_index}.#{pane_index}  #{pane_current_command}  #{pane_width}x#{pane_height}'[39m                                                                                                                                    
  It prints a line such as [38;5;153m%3  1.0  node  120x40[39m. The [38;5;153m%3[39m is the pane id. Pane ids don't change while the pane lives, so you only need to look it up again for new panes.                                                                                      
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              
  [1m3. Put the app into the state you want.[0m Switch to window 1 with [38;5;153mprefix + 1[39m, set up the screen as described in the list below, then switch back with [38;5;153mprefix + 2[39m. The app stays as it was. Avoid anything that animates, such as a spinner or a blinking      
  cursor, because the capture is a single frame.                                                                                                                                                                                                              
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              
  [1m4. Record it[0m from window 2:                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 
  [48;5;66mscripts/record-fixture.sh claude-code response-prose[49m %3                                                                                                                                                                                                     
  The arguments are [38;5;153m<app> <case> <pane-id>[39m. It prints [38;5;153mrecorded WxH -> ...[39m. If it says "refusing to overwrite", that case name is already used, so pick another.                                                                                               
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              
  [1m5. Check for secrets before moving on.[0m The files will be public in the open-source repo.                                                                                                                                                                    
  [36mcat[39m tests/fixtures/claude-code/response-prose.ansi                                                                                                                                                                                                          
  This shows the screen rendered. Look for API keys, tokens, emails, private repo or company names, and your home path. Then run:                                                                                                                             
  grep -a -n -i -E [31m'exampleusr|@|token|secret|password|api[_-]?key|sk-'[39m tests/fixtures/claude-code/response-prose.ansi                                                                                                                                        
  If something sensitive shows up, either re-record after changing what's on screen, or edit the [38;5;153m.ansi[39m file in an editor. If you edit, replace the text with the same number of characters (e.g. [38;5;153mxxxxx[39m), because column positions matter. Delete both files   
  and re-record if it's messy:                                                                                                                                                                                                                                
  [36mrm[39m tests/fixtures/<app>/<[94mcase[39m>.*                                                                                                                                                                                                                            
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              
  [1mWhat to record, with exact case names[0m                                                                                                                                                                                                                       
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              
  ┌─────┬────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐                                               
  │  #  │          Command           │                                                                         What to put on screen                                                                          │                                               
  ├─────┼────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤                                               
  │ 1   │ [38;5;153mclaude-code response-prose[39m │ A reply with prose long enough to wrap on 2 or more lines, a bullet list, and a fenced code block. Ask Claude something like "explain Rust lifetimes with an example". │                                               
  ├─────┼────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤                                               
  │ 2   │ [38;5;153mclaude-code diff[39m           │ A reply where Claude edited a file and the red and green diff is visible. Ask it to make a small edit in a throwaway repo.                                             │                                               
  ├─────┼────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤                                               
  │ 3   │ [38;5;153mclaude-code input-box[39m      │ A multi-line draft in the prompt box (use Shift+Enter or [38;5;153m\[39m plus Enter), with a tool-call block visible above it.                                                       │                                               
  ├─────┼────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤                                               
  │ 4   │ [38;5;153mlazygit default[39m            │ The default layout with a file selected, so the diff shows on the right.                                                                                               │                                               
  ├─────┼────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤                                               
  │ 5   │ [38;5;153mk9s pods[39m                   │ The pods table. If you don't have a cluster, skip this one and tell me.                                                                                                │                                               
  ├─────┼────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤                                               
  │ 6   │ [38;5;153mk9s logs[39m                   │ Press [38;5;153ml[39m on a pod to open its logs.                                                                                                                                     │                                               
  ├─────┼────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤                                               
  │ 7   │ [38;5;153mbtop main[39m                  │ The default view.                                                                                                                                                      │                                               
  ├─────┼────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤                                               
  │ 8   │ [38;5;153mvim split-numbers[39m          │ [38;5;153m:vsplit[39m with [38;5;153m:set number[39m, a different file in each half.                                                                                                               │                                               
  ├─────┼────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤                                               
  │ 9   │ [38;5;153mvim split-nonumber[39m         │ The same, after [38;5;153m:set nonumber[39m.                                                                                                                                         │                                               
  ├─────┼────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤                                               
  │ 10  │ [38;5;153mshell ls-and-wrap[39m          │ In a plain zsh pane, run [38;5;153mls -l[39m in a big directory, then [38;5;153mecho "$(seq 1 80 | tr '\n' ' ')"[39m so a long line wraps.                                                         │                                               
  └─────┴────────────────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘                                               
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              
  Don't feel you have to do all 10. Items 1 to 4 are the most valuable, and anything you can't run, just skip. Use throwaway content (a scratch repo, a dummy prompt) wherever you can, because then there's nothing to scrub.                                
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              
  [1mHanding them to me[0m                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              
  When you're done, run this to check what exists:                                                                                                                                                                                                            
  [36mls[39m -la tests/fixtures/*/                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    
  Then tell me which cases you recorded and any that were awkward, e.g. "k9s skipped, btop was mid-animation". I'll read the [38;5;153m.ansi[39m files, look at the raw escapes to see what each app emits, choose the probe positions, and generate the snapshots. If      
  you're unsure about a recording, record it anyway. It's cheap to delete.                                                                                                                                                                                    
                                                                                                                               
  The [38;5;153mUPDATE_FIXTURES[39m step isn't yours to run, because the probes in [38;5;153mexpected.json[39m are placeholders until I fill them in.      
                                                                                                                               
